{# ---------- Our story ---------- #}
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="story-title">
  <div class="container split">
    <div class="flow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Our story</p>
      <h2 class="mt-0" id="story-title">Three decades of global social work, one new office</h2>
      <p>The Steve Hicks School of Social Work first regularly placed students internationally in 1993, when MSSW interns joined UNHCR in Geneva. In the years since, students have been placed on every continent except Antarctica, and faculty-led internships for MSSW students have run in 20 countries.</p>
      <p>As Dean Allan Cole has noted, global engagement has been a part of the School's signature education landscape for more than 20 years. In 2023 the School brought that work together under a single office, charged with leading, supporting and coordinating the School's global education, research and service.</p>
      <ul class="stats">
        <li class="stat"><span class="stat__value">1993</span><span class="stat__label">First international placement, with UNHCR in Geneva</span></li>
        <li class="stat"><span class="stat__value">20</span><span class="stat__label">Countries with faculty-led MSSW internships</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <ol class="timeline">
        <li>
          <span class="timeline__year">1993</span>
          <p class="timeline__text">The School places its first MSSW interns with UNHCR in Geneva, beginning a partnership now in its fourth decade.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="timeline__year">2010</span>
          <p class="timeline__text">Projects with Underserved Communities launches with Texas Global and the Cockrell School of Engineering; around the same time, Maymester courses take social work students to Accra and London.</p>
          <!-- VERIFY: PUC launch year. Texas Global says 2010 (used site-wide); The Utopian says 2009. -->
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="timeline__year">c. 2015</span>
          <p class="timeline__text">The alliance with Pontificia Universidad Católica de Chile begins, a collaboration of about 11 years that produced Chile's first clinical master's degree in social work.</p>
          <!-- VERIFY: start year of the Chile alliance. Sources describe it only as an "~11-year alliance" (2026); confirm the year. -->
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="timeline__year">2023</span>
          <p class="timeline__text">The Office of Global Engagement is established. Dr. Rubén Parra-Cardona is appointed the School's first Associate Dean for Global Engagement, and Tanya Voss becomes Assistant Dean for Global Engagement.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="timeline__year">2024</span>
          <p class="timeline__text">Dr. Noël Busch-Armendariz is named Associate Dean for Global Engagement.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="timeline__year">2025</span>
          <p class="timeline__text">Writers and artists from the Seamus Heaney Centre at Queen's University Belfast join the School in Austin for "Constructive Dialogue, Poetry and Social Imagination."</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="timeline__year">2026</span>
          <p class="timeline__text">From Texas to the Troubles, OGE's signature program in Austin, Dublin and Belfast, launches in summer 2026.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- How we work ---------- #}
<section class="section section--sand" aria-labelledby="priorities-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section__head">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">How we work</p>
        <h2 class="section__title" id="priorities-title">Our strategic priorities</h2>
        <p class="section__intro">Four commitments guide the office's work with students, faculty, staff, alumni and partners.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <ul class="feature-list feature-list--2">
      <li><strong>Build international partnerships.</strong> We foster strategic partnerships on campus and with universities, agencies and organizations worldwide, from a decade-long alliance in Chile to peace and reconciliation work in Northern Ireland.</li>
      <li><strong>Enhance education on global social issues.</strong> We create and support opportunities for students to understand social issues in diverse cultural contexts through global practicums, signature programs and May Term courses.</li>
      <li><strong>Foster collaboration.</strong> We connect faculty with universities, research institutions and organizations around the world to develop innovative solutions to global social challenges.</li>
      <li><strong>Cultivate a community of international students and scholars.</strong> We support international students and visiting scholars at the School so that they thrive in Austin and connect with peers worldwide.</li>
    </ul>
